requirements:
Classifies pneumatic tyres into two distinct categories depending on service severity:
a) Type A — Heavy duty tyres (specifically recommended for load-carrying cycle rickshaws);
b) Type B — Standard duty tyres (recommended for conventional passenger cycles / bicycles).

Tyres are specified based on edge style to match various wheel rim profiles:
a) Wired Edge: Tyres mounted on straight side/wired-on rims;
b) Beaded Edge: Tyres mounted on hooked bead rims.

The structural casing cords must be manufactured from either:
a) Grey cotton yarn conforming to IS 7133;
b) Polyamide yarn/Nylon fabric conforming to IS 11573.

The welded joints of the steel bead wire must satisfy strict minimum ultimate breaking loads:
a) Type B (Standard Duty): Cotton Tyres require >= 128 kgf (1260 N); Nylon Tyres require >= 200 kgf (1960 N);
b) Type A (Heavy Duty): Cotton Tyres require >= 229 kgf (2250 N); Nylon Tyres require >= 400 kgf (3920 N).

Tyres must undergo continuous drum testing at a speed of 24 km/h under three progressive loading stages (Stage I, II, and III) at specified inflation pressures. For example:
a) Size 32-630 (at 480 kPa): Stage I = 72 kg, Stage II = 78 kg, Stage III = 84 kg;
b) Size 40-635 Type A (at 410 kPa): Stage I = 103 kg, Stage II = 111 kg, Stage III = 120 kg;
c) Size 40-635 Type B (at 410 kPa): Stage I = 86 kg, Stage II = 93 kg, Stage III = 100 kg.

To guide bicycle manufacturers in designing proper wheel fork and mudguard clearance envelopes, maximum service dimensions are calculated as:
a) Max Width: W_max = S + 3 mm (where S is design new section width);
b) Max Diameter: D_max = Dr + 2H + 6 mm (where Dr is nominal rim diameter and H is section height).
